{"retrieved_on": "2026-11-13", "source_url": "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=%28EXT_ID%3A21726217+OR+EXT_ID%3A21992749+OR+EXT_ID%3A21997792+OR+EXT_ID%3A22257669+OR+EXT_ID%3A22257792+OR+EXT_ID%3A22351925+OR+EXT_ID%3A22436890+OR+EXT_ID%3A22465077+OR+EXT_ID%3A22629234+OR+EXT_ID%3A22692650+OR+EXT_ID%3A22721175+OR+EXT_ID%3A22723499+OR+EXT_ID%3A22723603+OR+EXT_ID%3A22782003+OR+EXT_ID%3A22898692+OR+EXT_ID%3A22910935+OR+EXT_ID%3A22927533+OR+EXT_ID%3A22945569+OR+EXT_ID%3A23064544+OR+EXT_ID%3A23165123+OR+EXT_ID%3A23178227+OR+EXT_ID%3A23185978+OR+EXT_ID%3A23222703+OR+EXT_ID%3A23260099+OR+EXT_ID%3A23323831+OR+EXT_ID%3A23393430+OR+EXT_ID%3A23425165+OR+EXT_ID%3A23649456+OR+EXT_ID%3A23782923+OR+EXT_ID%3A23821585+OR+EXT_ID%3A24047337+OR+EXT_ID%3A24062559+OR+EXT_ID%3A24074941+OR+EXT_ID%3A24169273+OR+EXT_ID%3A24228906+OR+EXT_ID%3A24232462+OR+EXT_ID%3A24239921+OR+EXT_ID%3A24269113+OR+EXT_ID%3A24346241+OR+EXT_ID%3A24362405+OR+EXT_ID%3A24416692+OR+EXT_ID%3A24418598+OR+EXT_ID%3A24485249+OR+EXT_ID%3A24555472+OR+EXT_ID%3A24645774+OR+EXT_ID%3A24679531+OR+EXT_ID%3A24772210+OR+EXT_ID%3A24786629+OR+EXT_ID%3A24845019+OR+EXT_ID%3A24883008+OR+EXT_ID%3A24892406+OR+EXT_ID%3A24898551+OR+EXT_ID%3A24969913+OR+EXT_ID%3A24990346+OR+EXT_ID%3A25025374+OR+EXT_ID%3A25035207+OR+EXT_ID%3A25043041+OR+EXT_ID%3A25058905+OR+EXT_ID%3A25214542+OR+EXT_ID%3A25268160%29+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core&pageSize=100", "hitCount": 1, "resultList": {"result": [{"id": "22910935", "source": "MED", "pmid": "22910935", "pmcid": "PMC3723683", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC3723683"]}, "doi": "10.7326/0003-4819-157-4-201208210-00004", "title": "Predictive accuracy of the Liverpool Lung Project risk model for stratifying patients for computed tomography screening for lung cancer: a case-control and cohort validation study.", "authorString": "Raji OY, Duffy SW, Agbaje OF, Baker SG, Christiani DC, Cassidy A, Field JK.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Raji OY", "lastName": "Raji", "firstName": "Olaide Y", "initials": "OY", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Roy Castle Lung Cancer Research Programme, The University of Liverpool Cancer Research Centre, Institute of Translational Medicine, The University of Liverpool, Liverpool L3 9TA, United Kingdom."}]}}, {"fullName": "Duffy SW", "lastName": "Duffy", "firstName": "Stephen W", "initials": "SW"}, {"fullName": "Agbaje OF", "lastName": "Agbaje", "firstName": "Olorunshola F", "initials": "OF"}, {"fullName": "Baker SG", "lastName": "Baker", "firstName": "Stuart G", "initials": "SG"}, {"fullName": "Christiani DC", "lastName": "Christiani", "firstName": "David C", "initials": "DC"}, {"fullName": "Cassidy A", "lastName": "Cassidy", "firstName": "Adrian", "initials": "A"}, {"fullName": "Field JK", "lastName": "Field", "firstName": "John K", "initials": "JK", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3951-6365"}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3951-6365"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["recommended_reviews"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "4", "volume": "157", "journalIssueId": 1959096, "dateOfPublication": "2012 Aug", "monthOfPublication": 8, "yearOfPublication": 2012, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Ann Intern Med", "title": "Annals of internal medicine", "essn": "1539-3704", "issn": "0003-4819", "nlmid": "0372351", "isoabbreviation": "Ann Intern Med"}, "printPublicationDate": "2012-08-01"}, "pubYear": "2012", "pageInfo": "242-250", "abstractText": "<h4>Background</h4>External validation of existing lung cancer risk prediction models is limited. Using such models in clinical practice to guide the referral of patients for computed tomography (CT) screening for lung cancer depends on external validation and evidence of predicted clinical benefit.<h4>Objective</h4>To evaluate the discrimination of the Liverpool Lung Project (LLP) risk model and demonstrate its predicted benefit for stratifying patients for CT screening by using data from 3 independent studies from Europe and North America.<h4>Design</h4>Case-control and prospective cohort study.<h4>Setting</h4>Europe and North America.<h4>Patients</h4>Participants in the European Early Lung Cancer (EUELC) and Harvard case-control studies and the LLP population-based prospective cohort (LLPC) study.<h4>Measurements</h4>5-year absolute risks for lung cancer predicted by the LLP model.<h4>Results</h4>The LLP risk model had good discrimination in both the Harvard (area under the receiver-operating characteristic curve [AUC], 0.76 [95% CI, 0.75 to 0.78]) and the LLPC (AUC, 0.82 [CI, 0.80 to 0.85]) studies and modest discrimination in the EUELC (AUC, 0.67 [CI, 0.64 to 0.69]) study. The decision utility analysis, which incorporates the harms and benefit of using a risk model to make clinical decisions, indicates that the LLP risk model performed better than smoking duration or family history alone in stratifying high-risk patients for lung cancer CT screening.<h4>Limitations</h4>The model cannot assess whether including other risk factors, such as lung function or genetic markers, would improve accuracy. Lack of information on asbestos exposure in the LLPC limited the ability to validate the complete LLP risk model.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Validation of the LLP risk model in 3 independent external data sets demonstrated good discrimination and evidence of predicted benefits for stratifying patients for lung cancer CT screening. Further studies are needed to prospectively evaluate model performance and evaluate the optimal population risk thresholds for initiating lung cancer screening.", "affiliation": "Roy Castle Lung Cancer Research Programme, The University of Liverpool Cancer Research Centre, Institute of Translational Medicine, The University of Liverpool, Liverpool L3 9TA, United Kingdom.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Validation Study", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "P20 CA090578", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "CA090578", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "CA74386", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA092824", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "CA092824", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "P50 CA090578", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA074386", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Lung Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Tomography, X-Ray Computed"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Models, Statistical"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Risk Assessment"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Risk Factors"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Case-Control Studies"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Prospective Studies"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Decision Support Techniques"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Adult"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Aged"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Aged, 80 and over"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Middle Aged"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Referral and Consultation"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Female"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Male"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Early Detection of Cancer"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList